Body:
I understand. However, that would mean everyone's favourite theme should be built-in. That is not manageable. Also, theme updates would need to wait for opencode releases.

A theme plugin would be as simple as:
```json
{
  "name": "oc-plugin-bluloco",
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "engines": {
    "opencode": ">=1.3.7"
  },
  "themes": ["blu-loco.json"]
}
```

Theme paths like `blu-loco.json` will be resolved relative to `package.json`. Going forward plugins will be installable from github repos directly, so there is no need to publish an npm package. Users can let theme-only plugins auto-update if they so want or pin the version and manually update. It's then all up to the user and the community, without opencode releases or PRs blocking anything in this regard.
